the fields mostly use Kameez and a Tehband instead of Shalwar. In summer, l ight garments
are used as these are more comfortable. In winter, people use blankets or Loi to protect
themselves from cold. Some of the males wear turban . Generally, women wear bangles
(made up of glass or gold), finger -ring, a golden chain neck and ear -ring of different sizes,
color and design. The jewelry produced in the form of leaves, bracelets and nose -rings are
well known.
1.9 Languages
Urdu is the official language of the Government of AJ&K  which is mixture of Persian and
Arabic. Besides, Gojri, Kashmiri, Pahari, Pothohari, Hindku, D ogri and Punjabi are also
spoken in the State.
1.10 Food
Rice is the staple food of Kashmiries whereas  other favorite foods of Kashmiries are  wheat,
maize, meat, vegetables, etc. The manner of cooking is the same as in Pakistan. In the rural
areas of AJ&K, vegetable s are found in abundance while  subsidiary food is egg and fish.
During festivals, people cook P ulao, Zarda, Biryani, etc. Drinking water is also available

